                <pb facs="0153" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg45"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 7.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that the navy of Brazil has revolted, assumed complete
                    control over the harbors, and seized all the war vessels. It has made no attack
                    but threatens, unless the vice-president resigns, to bombard Rio de Janeiro.</p>
            </div>
